##
    A project that says only what to stop hearing.

    'ignore' silences a warning or an opinion across every file the project builds. It does not
    name anything to build, so a project made of nothing else is still empty — and being told
    it is empty is the useful thing to hear.

    The word after it names a severity or a diagnostic. A comment may begin with 'ignore' and
    stay a remark, because a comment is prose first; a project file has no prose, so the same
    words here are a mistake. It is reported and does not stop anything, since nothing about
    asking to hear less should be able to fail a build.
##

project QuietAndEmpty
    ignore whatever
end project
